{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Shaddai.</b> I am He whose divinity is sufficient (דַּי) for every creature; therefore walk before Me and I will be a god and patron to you. And so everywhere it appears in Scripture, its meaning is thus: 'sufficient of His,' all according to the context." "<b>Walk before.</b> As the Targum renders: serve before Me — cleave to My service." "<b>And be whole.</b> This too is a command after a command: be whole in all My trials. According to its midrash: 'Walk before Me' in the commandment of circumcision, and in this matter you shall be whole — for as long as the foreskin is on you, you are a blemished one before Me. Another matter: 'And be whole' — (now you are lacking five organs: two eyes, two ears, and the head of the body) — I will add a letter to your name, and the count of your letters will be 248, equal to the count of your organs."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:59.476083545Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}